#
# Conformance case: teleology/deontic-no-ideal-world (issue #1055 W1, Task 5).
#
# A deontic context that names a deontically-ideal world which is NOT accessible in the store (no ideal world to quantify over) → logic:GoalEvaluationUndetermined, NOT a vacuously-true obligation; contrasted with a second deontic context whose accessible ideal world satisfies the prescribed goal → obligation holds (Satisfied + Completed).
#
# CRITICAL: the teleology evaluator seeds ONLY from input.nq world facts; this
# input.logic.ttl carries the minimal, clean-compiling, certifiable program axiom
# the projections need (no asserted teleology triples here — the world facts live in
# input.nq, exactly as the foundation conformance cases keep theirs).

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/teleology/deontic-no-ideal-world/> .

ex:GoalExpression a logic:GoalExpression .
